=== PARITY (vs web GeofenceWidget.tsx) ===
  Data sources → bound via the shared state-holder seam (GeofenceStatusSource → Model):
    useGeofences (useLocations), useVehicles, useVehicleState, useUnits, useTranslation. The
    production app wires the source over the KMP locations/vehicle stores; the view does NO HTTP.
  Projection → GeofenceZoneProjection.build is a 1:1 port of the web useMemo:
    • haversineMeters (R=6_371_000) — verified 1° lon ≈ 111_194.9 m + identical-point 0 m.
    • hasCoords = vLat != 0 || vLon != 0 (web OR-guard, NOT AND) — unit-tested both-axes.
    • dist = hasCoords ? haversine : Infinity ; inside = dist <= (radius ?? 0).
    • currentZone = first inside && enabled (a disabled inside fence is skipped — tested).
    • coalescing name ?? '—', radius ?? 0, enabled ?? true (tested).
    • fmtRadius = fmtNumber(convertDistanceFromSI(m, unit), 1) + " " + unit (fixed-1-decimal;
      km/mi/ft suffix — tested, incl. non-finite defensive 0).
  Composition → glass shell (scope icon + "Geofence Status" title + freshness chip + refresh) ·
    1×2 compact (centered scope glyph + active-zone success chip OR neutral "No zone" — never
    blanks to an empty panel, matching the web compact return) · 2×4 standard (optional stale/
    offline banner + optional MapKit map when hasCoords && rows>=3 + scrollable fence list) ·
    fence row (name + "Radius: x" + Disabled/Inside(dot)/Outside chip + green active-zone tint).
  Shared components → Badge → GeofenceStatusChip (TSTone capsule, dot variant) ; EmptyState →
    ContentUnavailableView ("No geofences configured") ; maps Circle+Marker → MapKit
